    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Commands",
      "prov:value": "## Beyond the beans: other graphs in `lsi:near` (bean `ec2a`)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ec2a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Beyond the beans: other graphs in `lsi:near` (bean `ec2a`)",
      "prov:value": "`lsi:near` also searches every graph an instance declares under\n`lsiUnitProviders` in its `<instance>.json`: content **blocks** (core) and\n**Lean declarations** (sci). It prints **one list per graph**. Scores from two\nseparately built indexes are not comparable, so the lists are never merged\ninto one ranking (owner decision A, 2026-10-24; proposal\n`docs/proposals/lsi-cross-graph-near-2026-10-24.md`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-24",
        "docs/proposals/lsi-cross-graph-near-2026-10-24.md"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Cross-document links — a floor, and hubs reported, not penalised",
      "prov:value": "`bun run cat lsi links --instance <i> --graph <g>` proposes links between units of\nDIFFERENT documents in one graph: each unit's best other-document match, only\nat cosine ≥ 0.5 (`LINK_FLOOR`), with the units that are \"nearest\" to many\nothers listed as **hubs** to discount. On the IRIS replica it proposes 12 links and\nleaves 326 of 342 sections with none — the honest answer when the median best\nmatch is ~0.2."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Cross-document links — a floor, and hubs reported, not penalised",
      "prov:value": "**Why there is no hub PENALTY (bean `9udd`).** A CSLS-style penalty\n(`2·cos − r(a) − r(b)`) was measured on the 15 strongest the IRIS replica pairs a\nreader labelled, and made ranking worse: real-vs-spurious AUC 0.96 with plain\ncosine, 0.75–0.79 with the penalty at K = 5, 10, 20. The page it demoted most\n(HQ p36, mark-up) is central because it is genuinely on-topic. The floor alone\nis what the data supports; it is a house number fitted to 15 examples.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 9udd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Cross-document links — a floor, and hubs reported, not penalised",
      "prov:value": "## Keywords — the per-unit view the index used to discard (issue #2302)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2302"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Correspondence analysis — the parallel track",
      "prov:value": "[`correspondence-analysis`](../../../methodologies/correspondence-analysis.md)\nis a separate method over the same term matrix (`pipeline/ca.ts`):\nthe SVD of the χ² residuals, so no dimension carries document length or term\nfrequency. `bun run cat lsi:epics --method ca` runs it on the bean store.\n**Measured 2026-09-29: not significantly better or worse than LSI at filing\nbeans** (exact McNemar p = 0.17–0.71), so LSI stays the default. Reach for CA\nwhen an LSI dimension 1 has no negative pole, or when the question is which\nunits are UNUSUAL — CA's leading dimensions go to the most distinctive\nprofiles. Pick one per question; never average the two scores.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where to LOOK at an index",
      "prov:value": "`bun run cat lsi:viz` writes one page, `/cat-harness/lsi/` (\"Latent semantic\nindexes\"; `/lsi/` is its declared alias): every stored index with its\ndimensions as two poles, its findings, and the need-an-index verdicts.\ncat-harness DECLARES it — `visualisers` entry `lsi`, `covers: [\"qa\"]`,\n`renderedBy: lsi-viewer` — which since 2026-10-09 is how a directory's viewer\nis found; the page carries only `rendered-by: lsi-viewer` as provenance. So it appears on the navbar, the\nboard and the central **Published graphs** page (`/cat-harness/`, §\"Every\ndeclared viewer\") with no further wiring. `lsi:viz:check` fails in CI when the page is stale — so after\n`lsi index`, run `lsi:viz` too. The page is excluded from every index's units:\nindexing a page that reports on the indexes would never reach a fixed point.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the index lives, and what is stored",
      "prov:value": "That path is the **working copy, and nothing under it is committed** (bean\n`tqjj`, 2026-10-04 — the LSI subset of `5hox`). The record is the commit-keyed\nentry the CI job `qa-publish` stores on the orphan `qa-reports` branch\n(`main/<sha>/`, `pr/<n>/<sha>/`; arc `3fva`). The readers cope with its\nabsence (bean `oq1j`): with no `test/results/lsi/` in the checkout, the verdict\nrebuilds the index in memory and judges that run, writing nothing, and\n`lsi:viz` reads the indexes by ref through `qa-store` (`--ref`, default `main`)\n— anything but a hit exits 2 and writes no page about zero indexes.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean oq1j",
        "bean 3fva",
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the index lives, and what is stored",
      "prov:value": "The committed half reads **no index at all**: the verdict table is computed\nwith a source that holds nothing, so `graphVerdict` takes its compute-and-judge\nbranch over the current tree. That is not a detail. Were the table read from a\nstored index, the same commit would say `fresh` on a container holding a\nworking copy and `stale` in CI reading `qa-reports` at `main` — which resolves\nto the LATEST published entry, so the value would depend on when the gate ran\nrather than on the tree. **That is bean `in5a`'s loop arriving over the\nnetwork**, and it is the trap to avoid when taking any committed page off a\nstore: the page stops being a function of the tree.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean in5a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the index lives, and what is stored",
      "prov:value": "### Why a declared merge pattern was not enough, measured"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why a declared merge pattern was not enough, measured",
      "prov:value": "**State graphs are indexed on demand, never stored.** The `beans` graph\nchanges on nearly every commit; a stored index would be stale on every PR\nand a merge-conflict magnet. `lsi:epics` rebuilds it each run. That reasoning\nis now the general case rather than the exception: `skills` reached the same\nverdict for the same reason, three days later."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The same verdict in the audited record — `kg:audit`'s `tool-downstream-fresh`",
      "prov:value": "LSI is the first member of the **downstream-tool family** (bean `fq5u`). The\n`lsi-index` Tool node declares `downstream`, and every `bun run cat lsi index`\nwrites a `folio-tool-run/v1` record — outcome and input fingerprint, on\nsuccess AND on failure — under `test/results/tool-runs/lsi-index/`. The\nverdict reads three states:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean fq5u"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The same verdict in the audited record — `kg:audit`'s `tool-downstream-fresh`",
      "prov:value": "A sidecar on disk with no run record is `not-run`: a file is not evidence the\nrun that should keep it current succeeded. `kg:audit` carries this as\n`tool-downstream-fresh` on the `lsi-index` Tool (`minor`), one finding per\ngraph, using the same verdict function as `lsi:audit`. It generalises the\ngraph-level `lsi-index-fresh` it replaced. Its finding text carries **no\ncounts**, so the kg-qa sidecar moves only when a verdict flips."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The same verdict in the audited record — `kg:audit`'s `tool-downstream-fresh`",
      "prov:value": "A graph nobody has indexed yet (today: `cat-harness/docs`) is a standing\n`minor` finding on the `lsi-index` Tool. That is the point of recording it: \"needs one and has none\"\nis now a fact in the audited record instead of a line in a report."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Epic filing — the qou hierarchy, proposed by evidence",
      "prov:value": "It prints a **calibration line**: of the beans already under an epic, how\noften LSI's best guess is the current epic. Measured 2026-09-29: 145 / 247\n(59 %) against 21 classes, flat across k = 50–250, and log-entropy beat tf-idf\n(59 % vs 52 %). Read every proposal in that light.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-29"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Epic filing — the qou hierarchy, proposed by evidence",
      "prov:value": "**A disputed filing is not a misfiling.** The largest disputes on the first\nrun were beans filed by *symptom* (translation catalogues under CI\nRELIABILITY because they turned `main` red) that LSI files by *subject*\n(TRANSLATION). Both are defensible; which axis an epic means is a decision for\nthe owner, not for the score."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/lsi-indexing.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Reading a sidecar",
      "prov:value": "- **`retained`** — share of ‖A‖²_F the rank-`k` approximation keeps. It is not\n  a quality score; a low value on a large heterogeneous graph (beans: ~45 %)\n  is expected.\n- **Dimension 1 is usually a margin.** Qi et al. (2023): LSA's first\n  dimensions mainly carry document length and overall term frequency. A\n  dimension with no negative pole is that signature — skip it when reading\n  themes.\n- **`dimensions`** — a dimension is a *contrast*, so read the positive and\n  negative poles together. Refusal 2: it is not a topic until a person names\n  it.\n- **`narrowDimensions`** — a dimension ≥ 80 % of whose mass sits on ≤ 3 units\n  (or 1 %). Almost always non-prose: in the IRIS replica it found two different\n  kinds of placeholder text in the WPRO style guide on the first run —\n  Lorem-ipsum layout filler (pp. 21, 29–31) and pseudo-Latin font specimens\n  (pp. 14–15, 28). Treat as an ingestion finding.\n- **`nearDuplicates`** — cosine ≥ 0.95. In the bean store it found pairs such\n  as `3ozg`/`rmcf` (the same 72-sidecar churn, filed twice). A duplicate bean\n  is **scrapped with a pointer**, never deleted (`bean-coordination`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3ozg"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
